WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:18.628
It was early on a Thursday morning when Sherlock Holmes made up his mind.

2
00:00:18.648 --> 00:00:23.832
"Watson," he said to me over breakfast, "I have decided that I really must go after all."

3
00:00:23.852 --> 00:00:25.934
"Go! Where to?"

4
00:00:25.954 --> 00:00:32.299
"To Dartmoor to investigate the disappearance of Silver Blaze, the racehorse, and the murder of his trainer, John

5
00:00:32.339 --> 00:00:38.395
Straker." I was not surprised by Holmes' decision; in fact, I wondered why he hadn't gone sooner.

6
00:00:39.275 --> 00:00:43.858
For the past two days the great detective had been poring over the newspapers, which were filled with

7
00:00:43.898 --> 00:00:44.959
stories about the case.

8
00:00:45.939 --> 00:00:50.402
Silver Blaze, named for a white patch on his forehead, had been favored to win the Wessex Cup

9
00:00:50.462 --> 00:00:54.344
race. "I would be happy to go with you if I wouldn't be in the way," I said.

10
00:00:54.364 --> 00:01:00.248
"My dear Watson, you could help me a great deal by coming along and bringing your excellent binoculars.

11
00:01:01.288 --> 00:01:04.609
If we hurry, we just have time to catch our train at Paddington Station."

12
00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:10.592
And so I soon found myself sitting on a train speeding toward Dartmoor while Holmes read the latest

13
00:01:10.652 --> 00:01:15.154
newspapers. When he thrust the last one under the seat, he was ready to talk.

14
00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:21.236
"On Tuesday night I received telegrams from Colonel Ross, the horse's owner, and Inspector Gregory, who is in

15
00:01:21.296 --> 00:01:23.417
charge of the investigation," said Holmes.

16
00:01:23.437 --> 00:01:25.678
"They wanted my help with the case."

17
00:01:25.698 --> 00:01:27.339
"Tuesday night!

18
00:01:28.219 --> 00:01:29.660
Why didn't you go to Dartmoor yesterday?"

19
00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:35.202
"Because I made a mistake, which I do more often than people realize," admitted the great detective.

20
00:01:35.222 --> 00:01:41.405
"I thought it would be difficult to hide England's most famous racehorse, especially in such a sparsely inhabited

21
00:01:41.465 --> 00:01:46.747
place. At any moment I expected to hear that Silver Blaze had been found and that his abductor

22
00:01:46.827 --> 00:01:47.587
was the murderer.

23
00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:52.409
But all that has happened is that a young man named Fitzroy Simpson has been arrested."

24
00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:57.952
Although I had read some newspaper stories, Holmes wanted to go over the facts again with me.

25
00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:02.763
"Nothing clears up a case faster than describing it to another person," he explained.

26
00:02:03.644 --> 00:02:06.786
So I sat back while he gave me a summary of the events that had led to our

27
00:02:06.806 --> 00:02:13.692
journey. "Every precaution was taken to guard Silver Blaze at Colonel Ross' stable, which housed only four horses,"

28
00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:14.632
said Holmes.

29
00:02:14.652 --> 00:02:20.076
"Straker had worked for the colonel for a dozen years, first as a jockey and then as a

30
00:02:20.137 --> 00:02:24.420
trainer. He had always shown himself to be an honest and hard-working employee."

31
00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:29.563
The trainer and his wife lived with a maid in a small, red-brick house about two hundred yards

32
00:02:29.623 --> 00:02:30.264
from the stable.

33
00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:34.527
Besides Straker, there were three young grooms who worked with the horses.

34
00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.048
All three were trustworthy boys.

35
00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:42.392
One groom stayed up each night in the stable while the other two slept in the loft.

36
00:02:43.253 --> 00:02:45.234
The country around the stable was very lonely.

37
00:02:46.155 --> 00:02:49.877
About half a mile north was a cluster of houses, where travelers often stayed.

38
00:02:50.758 --> 00:02:53.340
The town of Tavistock lay two miles away to the west.

39
00:02:54.376 --> 00:02:58.578
Across the moor and also about two miles away was Mapleton, a larger training stable.

40
00:02:59.559 --> 00:03:02.821
Lord Brackwater owned this stable, and Silas Brown was the manager.

41
00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:07.743
Otherwise the moor was a complete wilderness, inhabited only by a few Gypsies.

42
00:03:08.724 --> 00:03:11.505
On Monday night Colonel Ross' stable was locked at nine o'clock.

43
00:03:12.426 --> 00:03:16.768
Two grooms went to Straker's house for supper while the third, Ned Hunter, remained on guard in the

44
00:03:16.808 --> 00:03:22.111
stable. The maid, Edith Baxter, was bringing him a supper of curried lamb when a young man suddenly

45
00:03:22.151 --> 00:03:23.352
appeared out of the darkness.

46
00:03:25.076 --> 00:03:29.657
He looked like a gentleman, dressed in a gray tweed suit with a red-and-black scarf and a cloth

47
00:03:29.717 --> 00:03:34.579
cap. She noticed that he was carrying a heavy walking stick with a large knob on top.

48
00:03:35.539 --> 00:03:36.519
"Stop, miss!"

49
00:03:36.879 --> 00:03:37.300
he called.

50
00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.060
"Can you tell me where I am?

51
00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.981
I had almost made up my mind to sleep on the moor when I saw the light of

52
00:03:43.021 --> 00:03:43.581
your lantern."

53
00:03:43.601 --> 00:03:47.022
"You are at Colonel Ross' stable," replied Edith.

54
00:03:47.042 --> 00:03:48.483
"What luck!"

55
00:03:48.903 --> 00:03:49.443
said the man.

56
00:03:49.463 --> 00:03:52.564
"I understand that a groom is on guard there every night.

57
00:03:53.356 --> 00:03:55.097
Perhaps that is his supper you are carrying."

58
00:03:55.938 --> 00:03:59.099
The man reached into his pocket and pulled out a folded piece of white paper.

59
00:03:59.119 --> 00:04:03.322
"See that the boy gets this, and I'll give you enough money to buy a new dress."

60
00:04:04.282 --> 00:04:08.144
The maid was afraid of the man and ran past him to the window, where she always handed

61
00:04:08.204 --> 00:04:08.725
in the meals.

62
00:04:10.385 --> 00:04:13.747
It was already open and Hunter was seated at a table inside the stable.

63
00:04:14.648 --> 00:04:17.770
She began to tell him what had happened when the stranger approached the window.

64
00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.111
"Good evening," he said to Hunter.

65
00:04:20.131 --> 00:04:22.012
"I want to have a word with you."

66
00:04:22.928 --> 00:04:24.128
"What business do you have here?"

67
00:04:24.489 --> 00:04:25.069
asked the boy.

68
00:04:25.089 --> 00:04:27.849
"It's business that could put money in your pocket.

69
00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:31.811
You have a horse running in the Wessex Cup race—Silver Blaze.

70
00:04:32.631 --> 00:04:34.191
What can you tell me about his chances?"

71
00:04:34.211 --> 00:04:37.492
"I won't give you any information," said Hunter.

72
00:04:37.512 --> 00:04:39.533
"Leave this property at once!"

73
00:04:40.573 --> 00:04:43.634
The groom quickly untied the dog and went out to chase the man away.

74
00:04:44.474 --> 00:04:45.694
But the man had disappeared.

75
00:04:46.655 --> 00:04:49.135
"One moment," I said, interrupting Holmes' story.

76
00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:52.969
"When the groom ran outside, did he leave the stable door unlocked?"

77
00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.331
"An excellent question, Watson.

78
00:04:56.212 --> 00:04:57.493
But no, he locked it."

79
00:04:59.095 --> 00:05:02.378
Hunter waited to tell Straker until the other grooms had returned from supper.

80
00:05:03.298 --> 00:05:06.681
Straker was upset by the story and around one o'clock in the morning Mrs.

81
00:05:06.721 --> 00:05:08.343
Straker awoke to find him dressing.

82
00:05:09.283 --> 00:05:11.565
He said that he was going out to check on Silver Blaze.

83
00:05:12.426 --> 00:05:14.288
She begged him not to go because it was raining.

84
00:05:15.209 --> 00:05:16.510
At seven o'clock, Mrs.

85
00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:18.992
Straker awoke and noticed that her husband had not returned.

86
00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:23.310
She and the maid set off for the stables where they found Hunter in some kind of stupor,

87
00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:26.372
Silver Blaze's stall empty, and no sign of her husband.

88
00:05:27.212 --> 00:05:28.713
The dog was asleep in its corner.

89
00:05:29.193 --> 00:05:31.715
Mrs. Straker quickly woke the two other grooms in the loft.

90
00:05:32.615 --> 00:05:35.517
They had heard nothing during the night because they were both sound sleepers.

91
00:05:36.497 --> 00:05:40.880
Hunter was obviously under the influence of some powerful drug, so he was left at the stable to

92
00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:45.422
recover. The two women and the two grooms ran out in search of Straker and the horse.

93
00:05:47.203 --> 00:05:50.877
About a quarter mile from the stable, Straker's coat was flapping from a bush.

94
00:05:51.797 --> 00:05:55.998
His dead body was nearby; he had been hit on the head with a heavy instrument and had

95
00:05:56.038 --> 00:05:57.238
a long cut on his thigh.

96
00:05:58.139 --> 00:06:01.480
Apparently he had tried to fight back because he had a small knife in his right hand.

97
00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:06.741
In his left hand he had the red-and-black scarf that the maid recognized as belonging to the stranger.

98
00:06:07.661 --> 00:06:11.602
From the hoofprints in the mud, it was easy to see that Silver Blaze had been there too.

99
00:06:11.622 --> 00:06:16.004
"Hunter was certain that the stranger had put something in his food while it was at the window,"

100
00:06:16.344 --> 00:06:16.844
said Holmes.

101
00:06:17.768 --> 00:06:22.553
"And indeed the food remaining on his plate was found to contain a large quantity of powdered opium.

102
00:06:23.454 --> 00:06:25.236
Everyone else who ate the curry was fine."

103
00:06:25.256 --> 00:06:27.278
"But what happened to the horse?"

104
00:06:27.698 --> 00:06:28.118
I asked.

105
00:06:29.039 --> 00:06:34.625
"Although Colonel Ross has offered a large reward," said Holmes, "Silver Blaze has not been seen since that

106
00:06:34.705 --> 00:06:34.965
night."
